<title>SINGAPORE: BATS 1996 net profit slips three pct.</title>
<headline>BATS 1996 net profit slips three pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  31.85    vs     32.93</p>
<p>Net final dividend (cts)	25.16    vs     24.82</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		 35.4     vs     36.6</p>
<p>    Turnover			  329.54     vs    337.72</p>
<p>    Interest income		   0.21     vs	0.04</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  0.16     vs	1.18</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		    46.66     vs     46.28</p>
<p>    Tax				  14.81     vs     13.35</p>
<p>    Dividend pay/register	  April 28/April 16</p>
<p>Note -- British-American Tobacco Company (Singapore) Ltd is involved in the manufacturing, import and sale of tobacco products. It said net profit was lower due to lower capital allowances and a provision for deferred taxation.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
